{"id": "EUVD-2026-104286", "enisaUuid": "b75c2cbd-419b-3ac8-bddc-e0a2402ce5ee", "description": "Krayin CRM before 2.2.7 contains a broken object level authorization vulnerability in EmailController write actions that allows scope-restricted authenticated users to manipulate other users' emails by supplying their numeric IDs. Attackers can call update, destroy, mass-update or mass-destroy endpoints to edit, re-send via is_draft=0, trash or permanently delete emails and disclose their subject, body and linked lead and person data.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:30:27", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/pull/2683", "https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/commit/64b9125f33a7eb2ef9916d0e5fd8215c7f6a8c28", "https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/blob/v2.2.6/packages/Webkul/Admin/src/Http/Controllers/Mail/EmailController.php", "https://github.com/krayin/laravel-crm/releases/tag/v2.2.7", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/krayin-crm-before-2.2.7-broken-object-level-authorization-in-mail-module"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112287", "GHSA-c5rj-qvgf-xg6f"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "64f52435-6e06-3f1f-8fda-255629e72bc2", "product": {"name": "laravel-crm", "vendor": {"name": "krayin"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "37d82818-f220-3202-9e73-88ef7bce938c", "vendor": {"name": "krayin"}}], "isExploited": false}